Markdown-native task tracking CLI designed for both humans and AI coding
assistants. Tasks live as plain .md files under tasks/ with YAML frontmatter
-- version-controlled alongside the code. Deterministic commands with stable
IDs and --json output, a validation gate, dependency graph, and a web
dashboard.

Agent Skills examples (one SKILL.md per workflow: do-task, split-task,
divide-and-conquer, import-todos, verify-task, ...) are installed under
share/examples/taskmd/skills/ -- copy or symlink them into a project's
.pi/skills/ to teach a coding agent the workflows.

Built from source for FreeBSD; upstream releases target macOS/Linux/Windows
only, so the optional web dashboard is not embedded in this package.
